{{also|jit|JIT|-jit-|jĭt|JİT|ji̍t}}

==Czech==

===Etymology===
{{inh+|cs|sla-pro|*jьti||to go}}.

===Pronunciation===
* {{cs-IPA}}
* {{audio|cs|Cs-jít.ogg|audio}}
* {{rhymes|cs|iːt|s=1}}

===Verb===
{{cs-verb|a=impf}}

# to [[walk]], [[go]] {{gloss|on foot}}
# to [[work]], [[do]], [[suffice]]
#: {{uxi|cs|Budou tři stačit? To '''půjde'''.|Will three be enough? It '''will do'''.}}
#: {{uxi|cs|'''Jde''' mi to.|I'm good at this.}}
# [[can]], to be [[possible]]
#: {{uxi|cs|'''Nejde''' udělat všechno dobře, ale alespoň udělat většinu dobře by už mohlo '''jít'''!|You can't do everything everything well, but you can do the most well!}}
# {{lb|cs|with the preposition {{m|cs|o}}}} to [[concern]], [[matter]], [[interest]] {{gloss|to be at issue, to be at stake}}
#: {{uxi|cs|'''Jde o''' život.|There's a life at stake.}}
#: {{uxi|cs|Právě '''o''' to mi '''jde'''.|That's exactly what I'm concerned about.}}

====Usage notes====
'''Jít''' is in the class of Czech [[concrete verb]]s. Its counterpart, {{l|cs|chodit}}, is an [[abstract verb]].

